 "issue_title": "Hardcoded optimization/validation ranges are physics-blind",
 "issue_body": "**Files:** `src/gui/tabs/optimization_tab.py:422,450,512,534`, `src/validation.py:338-339`, `src/gui/widgets/lens_editor.py:166,180`\n\nEditor allows `\u00b1100`, optimizer `\u00b120`, validator `\u00b1100`. Sag without diameter is meaningless (`R_vertex = r\u00b2/2\u00b7sag`, `src/lens.py:169`):\n- `D=5mm (r=2.5), sag=20` \u2192 `R=0.16mm`, slope ~80\u00b0 \u2014 violates `MIN_RADIUS`, TIRs.\n- `D=200mm (r=100), sag=20` \u2192 `R=250mm` \u2014 optimizer can't reach fast paraboloids.\n\n**Fix:** diameter-scale everywhere:\n```python\nr = lens.diameter / 2\nsag_max = min(0.5 * lens.diameter, 0.5 * lens.thickness + r*r/(2*Rmin))\nOptimizationVariable(..., -sag_max, sag_max)\n# validate_parabolic_sag(sag, diameter, thickness)\n```\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/228",
 "pr": 240,
 "pr_title": "fix(validation): scale parabolic sag limits by diameter",
 "pr_body": "Replace physics-blind hardcoded caps (editor +/-100, optimizer +/-20, validator +/-100) with diameter-scaled bounds from validation.parabolic_sag_limit().\r\n\r\n- validation: add parabolic_sag_limit() helper, extend validate_parabolic_sag() with optional diameter/thickness (legacy +/-100 cap preserved)\r\n- editor: sag spinboxes track live limit on load and diameter/thickness edits with clamp-back-to-model sync\r\n- optimizer: per-element scaled bounds for parabolic variables with legacy fallback\r\n- tests: 8 new cases for limit values, diameter-aware accept/reject, legacy cap, and GUI range tracking",
 "fix_commit": "8ddf2d9f94e1fd27a1641eaea8b52a37efe48d49",
